    fix: AUG-068 paginate declared-table selects past the 100-row page cap
    
    `select` sent the caller's query straight through, and DuckBrain caps a declared-table
    GET at 100 rows with NO truncation signal: a bare read returns one page, `limit=101`
    honours 101, `limit=1000` clamps at the server's hard cap, and a 200 carries no
    `Content-Range` and no `X-Total-Count` either way (re-probed live on this host). Equality
    between the rows returned and the limit asked for is the only signal the API offers, so a
    caller either pages or silently under-reports. `cmd_status` and `cmd_dump` read whole
    tables through `select` and did the latter: on `auger-df7-scale` (303 stored option rows,
    102 decisions at HEAD) `status` printed "options 100" and D-031 rendered two of its three
    options. Nothing was lost — every verb that counts, groups or renders rows was reading a
    truncated set.
    
    `select` and `select_or_empty` now page: an explicit `limit` + `offset` per request,
    stopping when a page comes back SHORT of the size it asked for — the one deterministic
    stop signal, and the property the fix is built on. `limit`-doubling is rejected in the
    code comment rather than merely not chosen: its page size depends on every earlier
    request, and its stop condition leans on the server clamping an oversized limit it never
    promised to clamp. A caller's own `limit` stays a CEILING on the result, so AUG-069's
    page-safe mint (`select=id&order=id.desc&limit=1`) is still ONE request per mint and still
    mints past the 100-decision mark; a table that is an exact multiple of the page is closed
    out by the first short page; `MAX_PAGES` bounds a server that ignores `offset` and refuses
    to return a partial read. `select_or_empty` stays all-or-nothing: a page that fails
    mid-read discards the pages before it instead of handing back half a table as "the table".
    
    Verified live (this host, HEAD + this change): a bare `option` read returns exactly 100
    rows while the paged read returns all 303, and `auger -n auger-df7-scale status` prints
    "decisions 102 | options 303" — matching a raw `limit=1000` read of the same tables.
    
    Tests: 10 new unit cases drive the REAL loop against a stand-in SERVER stubbed at `db`
    (one layer under `select`), which caps, clamps, filters and pages like the real one — RED
    before the fix, 6 of them failing on the single fetch; plus a live case storing the row's
    60 x 3 = 180-option shape in a throwaway namespace and asserting `status` counts 180 and
    `dump` renders all three of D-031's options. One AUG-069 live case was updated: its "a
    plain read caps at 100 rows" precondition now asserts the RAW read (the paged `select`
    returns 101), which is the premise the count mint froze on — the regression coverage the
    row asked to keep is intact and the boundary case still passes.
    
